=== (1) POSITIVE CONTROL — and it MUST be able to fail, so both sources are run ===
  from LABELS       : 0/7  []   <- v1's floor; the control CAN fail
  from QUESTION TEXT: 7/7  ['abdefect', 'abnomore', 'abhlth', 'abpoor', 'abrape', 'absingle', 'abany']
  GSS acts with BOTH sides (question text): ['abortion']
  ⇒ positive control fires: True  (floor 0/7 · observed 7/7)

=== (2) NEGATIVE CONTROLS — two, because the first one I wrote was MIS-SPECIFIED ===
  (2a) delete the 7 only            -> acts with both sides: ['abortion']
       ⚠ **this control was WRONG and its failure is informative, not a defect**: GSS carries
       **14** items the detector
       marks LEGAL for abortion, not 7 — the split-ballot `*g` twins, `ablegal`, and others.
       Deleting a SUBSET of the signal and demanding the verdict flip is not a control.
  (2b) delete EVERY named abortion-legal item (14) -> []  ⇒ abortion's legal side gone: True

=== (2c) THE LEAK CONTROL — the one that earned itself, and it is QUANTITATIVE ===
  v1 (no STOP condition):   84 inheritances, **  41 across a name-prefix boundary**
  v2 (clears on any non-continuation):   28 inheritances, **   3 across a boundary**
  ⇒ leak control passes: True   (floor = v1's 41; a smear is measurable, not felt)

